<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 25 November, from 571 BCE to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/servius-tullius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">571 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,596 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Servius Tullius celebrates a triumph over the Etruscans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to the Fasti Triumphales, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius">Servius Tullius</a>, by tradition the sixth king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, celebrated the first of three triumphs over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>. He is said to have routed a great Etruscan army early in his reign.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius">Servius Tullius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph">Roman triumph</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1034">1034 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">992 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malcolm II of Scotland dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malcolm II died after a 29-year reign and was succeeded by his grandson Duncan I. Duncan was killed in battle by Macbeth in 1040, events Shakespeare reworked freely more than five centuries later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1120 CE <span class="tih-ago">906 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The White Ship sinks off Barfleur, drowning William Adelin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The White Ship sank in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a> off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barfleur">Barfleur</a>, drowning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-adelin">William Adelin</a>, heir to Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>; of some 300 aboard, only a butcher from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a> survived. William's death led to the Anarchy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-adelin">William Adelin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1177">1177 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">849 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baldwin IV of Jerusalem routs Saladin at Montgisard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The young King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-iv-of-jerusalem">Baldwin IV of Jerusalem</a>, a leper since childhood, with a small force of knights including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon">Raynald of Châtillon</a>, surprised and routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s much larger army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a>. Saladin narrowly escaped back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-montgisard">Battle of Montgisard</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-iv-of-jerusalem">Baldwin IV of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon">Raynald of Châtillon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1491">1491 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">535 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Boabdil agrees to surrender Granada to Ferdinand and Isabella</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Muhammad XII (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-xii-of-granada">Boabdil</a>) agreed in the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> to surrender Granada to Ferdinand and Isabella, who guaranteed the Muslims their religion, law and property. The city was handed over on 2 January 1492; the promises were broken within a decade.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-granada-1491">Treaty of Granada (1491)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The last British troops leave New York City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British forces evacuated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, their last stronghold in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> led the Continental Army into the city. 'Evacuation Day' was celebrated in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> for over a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union troops storm Missionary Ridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Chattanooga, Union soldiers charged up Missionary Ridge beyond their orders and routed Braxton Bragg's Confederate army. The victory opened the way into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hollywood studios blacklist the 'Hollywood Ten'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Studio heads issued the Waldorf Statement, refusing to employ ten writers and directors cited for contempt of Congress. The Hollywood blacklist that followed ended or interrupted hundreds of careers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suriname gains independence from the Netherlands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Guiana on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>'s north coast became the independent Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>. Around a third of its population emigrated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 November <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yelu-deguang"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Yelü Deguang</span><span class="tp">902–947</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-jin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-taizong-of-jin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Taizong of Jin</span><span class="tp">1075–1135</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/catherine-cornaro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/catherine-cornaro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Catherine Cornaro</span><span class="tp">1454–1510</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lope-de-vega"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lope-de-vega.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lope de Vega</span><span class="tp">1562–1635</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/piet-heyn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/piet-heyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Piet Heyn</span><span class="tp">1577–1629</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/catherine-of-braganza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/catherine-of-braganza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Catherine of Braganza</span><span class="tp">1638–1705</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernest-louis-grand-duke-of-hesse"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernest-louis-grand-duke-of-hesse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernest Louis, Grand Duke of Hesse</span><span class="tp">1868–1937</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludvik-svoboda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludvik-svoboda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludvík Svoboda</span><span class="tp">1895–1979</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/augusto-pinochet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Augusto Pinochet</span><span class="tp">1915–2006</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 November <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bilge-qaghan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bilge-qaghan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bilge Qaghan</span><span class="tp">d. 734</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/malcolm-ii-of-scotland"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Malcolm II of Scotland</span><span class="tp">c. 954–1034</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-adelin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-adelin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Adelin</span><span class="tp">1103–1120</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andrea-doria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andrea-doria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andrea Doria</span><span class="tp">1466–1560</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-xii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso XII</span><span class="tp">1857–1885</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prince-george-of-greece-and-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prince-george-of-greece-and-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prince George of Greece and Denmark</span><span class="tp">1869–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/u-thant"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/u-thant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">U Thant</span><span class="tp">1909–1974</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hastings-banda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hastings-banda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hastings Banda</span><span class="tp">c. 1898–1997</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fidel-castro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fidel Castro</span><span class="tp">1926–2016</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
